{#- The thing that was missing, and the reason granting somebody a role did
   not make one appear: a role says what a person may DO, a partner is the
   ministry whose supporters and goals they manage. Sending a new person is
   two acts, and this is the second. -#}

<form class="ms-form adm-form" id="admPartnerForm" hidden>
  <div class="ms-grid">
    <label class="fld">
      <span data-i18n="adm.partnerName">Name</span>
      <input type="text" id="admPartnerName" maxlength="200" required>
    </label>
    <label class="fld">
      <span data-i18n="adm.partnerFor">Who is it for</span>
      <select id="admPartnerUser"></select>
    </label>
  </div>
  <div class="ms-actions">
    <button type="submit" class="solid-btn" data-i18n="adm.create">Create</button>
    <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="admPartnerCancel" data-i18n="ms.cancel">Cancel</button>
  </div>
</form>

{#- THE ORGANIZATION'S OWN MAIL, above the ministries rather than as one of
   them. Nothing else on a partner card applies to Thauma itself, and a card
   with one working control and four dead ones invites somebody to try them.

   It is here because there was nowhere else. thauma.one sends the account
   invites and the sign-up confirmations everybody depends on, and its
   addresses have to be maintained by the same person maintaining everybody
   else's — on the same screen, so the whole picture is in one place. -#}
{#- The whole card is rendered by the console, because its summary row has to
   count addresses that only arrive with the data. Left empty here rather than
   half-built in markup and half in script, which is the arrangement that
   guarantees the two drift. -#}
<div id="admOrgMail"></div>

